      "markdown": "Royal Hospital Chelsea, London SW3\n\n# Masterpiece London 2019\n\nA bespoke, hand-crafted wallcovering in bold abstract shapes, installed on a stand at the Masterpiece London art fair in June 2019.\n\n![Bold abstract hand-crafted wallcovering on a stand at Masterpiece London 2019.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/masterpiece-04-800.webp)\n\n## Project record\n\nClient, materials & project facts\n\n**Client**\n: An exhibitor at Masterpiece London\n\n**Designer**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Main contractor**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Maker and paper**\n: Bespoke hand-crafted wallcovering\n\n**Area or rooms**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Scope**\n: Installation of a bespoke hand-crafted wallcovering on an exhibition stand\n\n**Year**\n: 2019\n\nMasterpiece London was the summer art and antiques fair in the grounds of the Royal Hospital Chelsea. In June 2019 we installed a bespoke, hand-crafted wallcovering on one of its stands: bold abstract shapes in teal, red and blue, outlined in gold.\n\n## At a glance\n\n- **Where:** Masterpiece London 2019, Royal Hospital Chelsea\n- **When:** June 2019\n- **Scope:** installation of a bespoke hand-crafted wallcovering on an exhibition stand\n- **Set-out:** laser levels\n\n## A fair stand\n\nA fair stand is built and dressed in days, and it is seen close up by every visitor. A hand-crafted design has no repeat to fall back on, so each panel is placed where the design needs it, set out with laser levels so the outlines run through from one panel to the next.\n\n## Photographs on this page\n\nOur own photographs, first posted on our Instagram, [@mrwallcover](https://www.instagram.com/mrwallcover/), on 21 and 26 June 2019 ([first post](https://www.instagram.com/p/By-zBigFOAR/), [second post](https://www.instagram.com/p/BzLSNUKFouL/)). The exhibitor is not named.\n\n## Photographs\n\n![Bespoke hand-crafted wallcovering with sweeping gold outlines, Masterpiece London 2019.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/masterpiece-02-800.webp)\n\n![Laser levels, knives and tools laid out for the installation at Masterpiece London 2019.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/masterpiece-01-800.webp)\n\nHow the commission ran\n\n## The same standards, on every commission.\n\nEach commission has a written scope by room, walls prepared until they are true, protected floors, batch and shade control, set-out from the room’s focal points, and a return visit. [Read the method](https://www.mrwallcover.com/practice/#method).\n\nThe six standards in full\n\n01\n\n### Survey and scope, room by room\n\nWe measure the wall that will actually be hung, allow for the repeat and the wastage, and write a scope of works room by room before anyone orders paper.\n\n02\n\n### Preparation decides the finish\n\nWalls are filled, made good and primed until they are true. If a wall is not ready for the material specified, we say so before the last drop is ordered.\n\n03\n\n### Protection and containment\n\nFloors, furniture and finished joinery are protected as part of the hang. Work is contained and the place is left tidy each evening. In a home we are visitors; in a hotel we work around the house.\n\n04\n\n### Batch and shade control\n\nDeliveries are checked against the measure, and batches and shading are managed so that a corridor of rooms reads as one surface.\n\n05\n\n### Set out from the room's focal points\n\nPattern is set out from chimneypieces, doorcases and bed walls, so the pattern sits square to the cornice and the joinery.\n\n06\n\n### One team, then the return visit\n\nThe people who start are the people who finish. Four to six weeks after completion we come back to look at every seam and edge, and the workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months.\n\n[See the finish up close: seams, internal corners, edges and joins from our own installations](https://www.mrwallcover.com/details/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last updated 22 October 2026\n",
